WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:02.827
Our algorithm closes the
planning–learning loop.

2
00:00:04.250 --> 00:00:08.965
Model predictive control plans robot
actions using a learned world model.

3
00:00:08.990 --> 00:00:13.445
The model predicts action outcomes,
while a critic estimates future return.

4
00:00:13.470 --> 00:00:16.682
The robot executes one action, then
replans.

5
00:00:19.250 --> 00:00:21.525
The policy proposes actions.

6
00:00:21.550 --> 00:00:24.025
Aligning it with the planner leaves
three issues:

7
00:00:24.050 --> 00:00:28.405
delayed reward propagation, uncertain
terminal values, and differences in

8
00:00:28.430 --> 00:00:29.656
episode quality.

9
00:00:31.250 --> 00:00:35.045
Our algorithm changes three learning
signals while keeping the world model

10
00:00:35.070 --> 00:00:36.771
and planning optimizer.

11
00:00:38.250 --> 00:00:40.765
The baseline uses one-step targets.

12
00:00:40.790 --> 00:00:43.653
Our algorithm uses hybrid multi-step
targets.

13
00:00:44.250 --> 00:00:48.487
Experience updates the model, critic,
and policy for future plans.

14
00:00:49.250 --> 00:00:53.265
Hybrid multi-step temporal-difference
targets use several rewards to teach

15
00:00:53.290 --> 00:00:55.005
earlier decisions.

16
00:00:55.030 --> 00:00:59.225
We take available rewards from replay,
extend the sequence with the model,

17
00:00:59.250 --> 00:01:00.946
and then bootstrap from the critic.

18
00:01:04.250 --> 00:01:08.405
Adaptive terminal estimates lower the
online terminal value when target

19
00:01:08.430 --> 00:01:10.185
critics disagree.

20
00:01:10.210 --> 00:01:14.485
A larger disagreement means a larger
penalty, reducing the influence of

21
00:01:14.510 --> 00:01:16.534
uncertain values on planning.

22
00:01:17.250 --> 00:01:20.967
Return-weighted actor distillation gives
higher-return episodes more

23
00:01:20.992 --> 00:01:22.998
influence on imitation.

24
00:01:23.023 --> 00:01:25.884
It uses realized episode returns.

25
00:01:25.909 --> 00:01:29.487
After a fixed warmup, the extra loss
helps the policy learn from planner

26
00:01:29.512 --> 00:01:30.663
